{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent legal battles that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher, and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his sharp and witty dialogue. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook, along with andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake as sean parker.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright, played by rooney mara. this event sets off a chain reaction, as mark creates a website called \"facemash\", which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nlater, mark is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss, two twin brothers who are also students at harvard, to create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but eventually drops out and creates his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\". the site quickly gains popularity, and mark becomes an overnight sensation.\n\nhowever, the success of the site also leads to a series of legal battles, as the winklevoss brothers claim that mark stole their idea, and eduardo saverin, who was initially a partner in the project, claims that mark cheated him out of his share of the company. the movie follows the story of these legal battles, as well as the personal struggles of mark zuckerberg, who becomes increasingly isolated and alone as the site grows in popularity.\n\nthe movie features strong performances from the entire cast, with jesse eisenberg standing out as mark zuckerberg. the film also features a great soundtrack, which includes music by trent reznor and atticu